    "body": "## Motivation\n\nTwo small issues in the MiniMax-M3 sparse decode launcher (`minimax_sparse/decode/topk_sparse.py`):\n\n1. The autotune key of `_gqa_share_sparse_decode_kernel` lists `\"block_size\"`, which is not a kernel argument (the kernel takes `BLOCK_SIZE_N`). Triton's `Autotuner.run` keeps only key names that are kernel arguments (`[_args[key] for key in self.keys if key in _args]`), so the entry is silently dropped. `PAGED_CONTIG` is not in the key either. Both select different compiled kernels, so a config tuned for one block size or KV layout is reused for another. Within one serving process both are fixed today, so this does not change current results; it does when they vary in one process (tests, multiple models).\n2. When `NUM_TOPK_CHUNKS == 1` the merge kernel still launches, although merging one chunk is an identity: `weights = exp(lse - lse) / 1 = 1`. With one KV head per rank (MiniMax-M3 at TP4 and TP8) this is every decode step at batch size > 128.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Key on `BLOCK_SIZE_N` and `PAGED_CONTIG` instead of the nonexistent `block_size`. Tensor dtypes (bf16 vs fp8 KV) were already part of the key through Triton's automatic dtype entries.\n- Return the single chunk directly when `NUM_TOPK_CHUNKS == 1`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNew `test/registered/kernels/ops/attention/test_minimax_sparse_decode_chunks.py` compares the kernel with a torch fp32 reference at the per-rank MiniMax-M3 shape (16 q heads, 1 KV head, head_dim 128, block 128, top-16), at batch 4 (several chunks, merge runs) and batch 256 (one chunk, merge skipped). Registered for CUDA (`base-b-kernel-unit`, next to the sibling tests) and AMD (`stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd`). 2 passed on MI355X.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nMI355X (gfx950), ROCm 7.2.0, torch 2.9.1, Triton 3.7.0. One `flash_decode_with_gqa_share_sparse` call at the TP4 per-rank shape, 8k context, page size 128; `triton.testing.do_bench` median, minimum of 5 repetitions:\n\n| Batch | Chunks | `main` (µs) | This PR (µs) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 32 | 8 | 53.3 | 53.0 |\n| 64 | 4 | 49.6 | 49.0 |\n| 128 | 2 | 62.1 | 62.0 |\n| 256 | 1 | 98.5 | 95.6 |\n| 512 | 1 | 154.6 | 149.4 |\n\nAbout 3% per sparse layer once the batch has a single chunk (57 sparse layers in MiniMax-M3); no change below that, as expected.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not needed.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37914124295](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37914124295)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37914123893](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37914123893)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37914124425](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37914124425)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
